ABSTRACT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The cosmological constant problem is the 120-order-of-magnitude gap between
the naive quantum-field-theory vacuum energy density rho_vac ~ M_P^4 and
the observed dark energy density rho_Lambda ~ 2.5e-47 GeV^4. The Hodge
Complex Standard Model has, since HCSM-53, derived the value
rho_DE = (d+1)/2 * m_nu^4 from the residual vacuum energy of the
self-canceling 8x8 torus, matching observation to 0.76%, or to 0.010% with
the refined formula of HCSM-52. What has not been established is the
physical mechanism by which the residual is promoted to the observed
cosmological constant. This sub-paper closes that open item (item 6.13).
We prove that the promotion is a PURE PROJECTION, not a coupling to
gravity.

The five-layer loop M_loop = T * L_EFT * L_Core * L_DME * L_FDLM acts on
the 14-mode multiplet; the EFT layer L_EFT acts as a soft projector with
weight 1 + c * delta, where c = 5/9 is fixed by the Kernel-Diagonal
Theorem (HCSM-14.a); the residual energy projects onto the timelike
direction of ker D with unit weight; and the hidden u(1) VEVs vanish at
machine precision. The combined result is that no gauge mediator exists
between the hidden and visible sectors (HCSM-41, epsilon = 0 exactly), no
gravitational suppression factor 1/M_P^2 is present, and the residual
vacuum energy becomes the observed cosmological constant by projection
alone. All numerical claims are verified at machine precision.

