--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 The hidden sector
---------------------

By HCSM-38, the hidden sector at lambda = 4 is the 42-dimensional content

    H = Omega^1 | lambda=4  +  Omega^2 | lambda=4
    dim H = 28 + 14 = 42

with D_4 decomposition

    H = 6 A_1 + 4 A_2 + 5 B_1 + 5 B_2 + 11 E

By HCSM-39, the hidden sector is U(1)_Y-neutral.

4.2 The four hidden u(1) generators
-----------------------------------

The HCSM gauge algebra is

    su(3)_c + su(2)_L + u(1)^5

The five u(1) factors split into the visible hypercharge u(1)_Y and four
hidden factors u(1)^4_hid. Each hidden u(1) generator acts as a traceless
diagonal operator on the multiplicity space of each D_4 irrep block of the
hidden sector.

4.3 The hidden vacuum
---------------------

By HCSM-39 Disclosed Choice 2, the hidden sector is U(1)_Y-neutral. The
natural hidden vacuum is the symmetric (maximally mixed) state in each D_4
multiplicity space:

    |0>_m = (1/sqrt(m)) sum_{i=1}^m |i>_m

where m is the multiplicity of the irrep block.

Theorem 3 (Hidden VEVs vanish).
For each hidden u(1) generator h_i (i = 1, 2, 3, 4),

    <0 | h_i | 0> = 0

Proof.
Each h_i is traceless on each D_4 multiplicity space; the hidden vacuum is
uniform on each space. Therefore

    <0_m | h_i | 0_m> = (1/m) sum_{k=1}^m (h_i)_kk = (1/m) Tr(h_i) = 0

This holds for each irrep block A_1, A_2, B_1, B_2, E; summing over blocks
preserves the vanishing.  []

Corollary.
The hidden u(1) factors contribute zero to the residual vacuum energy:

    delta_rho_hidden = 0

Proof.
The vacuum contribution of a u(1) factor to the residual energy is
proportional to the square of its VEV. Since all VEVs vanish, all hidden
contributions vanish.  []

Remark (Falsification).
The hidden-VEV result would be falsified if the hidden vacuum were not the
symmetric state (e.g., if a hidden-sector Higgs mechanism broke the hidden
u(1)s), or if a hidden u(1) generator had a nonzero trace component (a
central element that was not modded out). Neither holds in the current HCSM
construction; the result is structural.

