7. FALSIFICATION TESTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    (1) rho_DE value. The refined prediction is
        rho_DE = 2.5003e-47 GeV^4. A measured value outside the interval
        [2.4995, 2.5015]e-47 GeV^4 falsifies the projection mechanism.

    (2) Timelike projection weight. The weight is exactly 1; a deviation to
        1/4 (or to any other value) would falsify Theorem 4.

    (3) Hidden VEVs vanish. A confirmed nonzero hidden u(1) VEV (e.g., from
        hidden-sector Higgs breaking) would falsify Theorem 3.

    (4) No gauge mediator. A confirmed dark photon with epsilon > 1e-12
        (HCSM-41) would falsify the projection mechanism by opening a gauge
        channel.

    (5) Equation of state. HCSM predicts w = -1 exactly at leading order,
        with EFT correction w = -1.014054... A measured time dependence of
        rho_DE at leading order would falsify the topological
        interpretation.

